---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import release from "../../../data/release.json";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Roadmap — Burnished Sky Ahead"
  description="Creator-curated public roadmap for future Burnished Sky Ahead updates."
  current="roadmap"
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Creator-curated, released for everyone</p>
      <h1>Roadmap</h1>
      <p class="lede">Download milestones, Store reviews, and support messages help inform future free updates; devjoe curates the final scope.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="content-grid">
      <aside>Release milestones</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Every milestone is for everyone.</strong> Reaching a download target begins evaluation; it does not promise a delivery date or grant an individual unlock, vote, or priority response.</p>
          <p>Download targets match the public Connect IQ Store tiers—1K+, 10K+, and 50K+—so each milestone can be observed without an unpublished exact count.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="milestone-list">
          {release.milestones.map((milestone) => (
            <article class="milestone">
              <div class="milestone-id">{milestone.id}</div>
              <div>
                <strong>{milestone.downloads.toLocaleString("en-US")} downloads</strong><br />
                <span class="status-tag">{milestone.status}</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3>{milestone.feature}</h3>
                <p>{milestone.description}</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
        <h2>How decisions are made</h2>
        <p>
          devjoe sets the milestones and final scope while actively reading Store
          reviews and messages from supporters. Aggregate progress is updated
          manually. Supporter names and messages remain private unless the person
          explicitly approves publication.
        </p>
        <p>States move from Target not reached → Target reached → In design → In testing → Released.</p>
        <h2>{release.support.goal.title}</h2>
        <p>{release.support.goal.purpose}</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Separate from the roadmap.</strong> {release.support.goal.disclaimer} Ko-fi progress cannot change a feature's milestone state.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
